{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**PARAGRAPH 1**\n\n\"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS A STATEMENT THAT CHALLENGES THE FUNDAMENTAL PRINCIPLE OF THE RULE OF LAW. LAWS ARE CREATED TO MAINTAIN ORDER, PROTECT RIGHTS, AND ENSURE JUSTICE WITHIN A SOCIETY. WHEN INDIVIDUALS BEGIN TO PICK AND CHOOSE WHICH LAWS TO OBEY BASED ON PERSONAL JUDGMENT, IT UNDERMINES THE STABILITY AND PREDICTABILITY THAT LAWS ARE DESIGNED TO PROVIDE. THIS STATEMENT COULD ENCOURAGE ANARCHY BY LEGITIMIZING DISOBEDIENCE BASED ON SUBJECTIVE MORAL OR POLITICAL BELIEFS.\n\n**PARAGRAPH 2**\n\nADDITIONALLY, THE ASSERTION THAT ONE SHOULD NOT FOLLOW A \"BAD\" LAW LACKS A DEFINITION OF WHAT CONSTITUTES A LAW AS \"BAD.\" WITHOUT CLEAR CRITERIA, THIS STATEMENT BECOMES SUBJECTIVE AND COULD BE USED TO JUSTIFY ANY FORM OF DISOBEDIENCE, INCLUDING THOSE THAT HARM OTHERS OR DISRUPT SOCIETAL HARMONY. EVEN IF A LAW IS PERCEIVED AS UNFAIR OR OUTDATED, THERE ARE ESTABLISHED LEGAL AND POLITICAL CHANNELS FOR CHALLENGING IT, SUCH AS COURT APPEALS OR LEGISLATIVE REFORMS. RELYING ON INDIVIDUAL DISCRETION OVER LAW COMPLIANCE ERODES THE COLLECTIVE TRUST IN INSTITUTIONS THAT GOVERN A FUNCTIONING SOCIETY.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -1.3133596181869507}, {"token": "PAR", "logprob": -3.3378546504536644e-06}, {"token": "AG", "logprob": -9.059865078597795e-06}, {"token": "RAP", "logprob": -0.00013410145766101778}, {"token": "H", "logprob": -3.4570634852570947e-06}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.040434613823890686}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -4.327203714638017e-05}, {"token": "**\n\n", "logprob": -1.4104558229446411}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.5938528776168823}, {"token": "IF", "logprob": -0.001578276976943016}, {"token": " THE", "logprob": -0.00032610344351269305}, {"token": " LA", "logprob": -0.0002441108226776123}, {"token": "W", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": " IS", "logprob": -1.120561046263